io tolerances or HID mappings.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Check Xone:96 official manual, ports and operating mode.","Exercise all eq controls or signal routes using MIDI monitor, DJ software or external measurement as appropriate.","Repeat, save evidence and distinguish unobservable from failed hardware."],"equipment":["Device","Compatible host or measurement interface as needed"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"allen-and-heath-xone-96-audio","category":"audio","title":"Audio output channel integrity","why":"Test actual hardware response without inventing MIDI IDs, audio tolerances or HID mappings.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{},"steps":["Check Xone:96 official manual, ports and operating mode.","Exercise all audio controls or signal routes using MIDI monitor, DJ software or external measurement as appropriate.","Repeat, save evidence and distinguish unobservable from failed hardware."],"equipment":["Device","Compatible host or measurement interface as needed"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"allen-and-heath-xone-96-usb","category":"usb","title":"USB discovery and reconnect","why":"Test actual hardware response without inventing MIDI IDs, audio tolerances or HID mappings.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Check Xone:96 official manual, ports and operating mode.","Exercise all usb controls or signal routes using MIDI monitor, DJ software or external measurement as appropriate.","Repeat, save evidence and distinguish unobservable from failed hardware."],"equipment":["Device","Compatible host or measurement interface as needed"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"allen-and-heath-xone-96-version","category":"software","title":"Firmware and software compatibility","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Inspect device model and installed firmware.","Check exact model's official support page for updates and compatible software.","Record version, OS, source and date."],"equipment":["Manufacturer documentation"],"severity":"minor","pass":null},{"id":"allen-and-heath-xone-96-verified-dual-usb","category":"software","title":"Dual USB audio path and device selection","why":"Validate this manufacturer-documented feature using a known-good signal or application.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Connect separate computers to USB1 and USB2.","Run known-good stereo test signal through each interface and route to mixer.","Confirm each USB stream and headphone cue independently."],"equipment":["Device","Known-good test signal or compatible software"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"allen-and-heath-xone-96-verified-filters","category":"mixer","title":"VCF mode, resonance and CRUNCH","why":"Validate this manufacturer-documented feature using a known-good signal or application.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Feed reference audio through each of the two assignable VCF units.","Switch HPF, BPF and LPF; sweep frequency and resonance.","Engage CRUNCH and verify the distortion path is present only as intended."],"equipment":["Device","Known-good test signal or compatible software"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"allen-and-heath-xone-96-verified-midi","category":"midi","title":"Published MIDI switch mapping and channel selection","why":"Validate this manufacturer-documented feature using a known-good signal or application.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Open the official Xone:96 MIDI implementation document.","Capture CUE and input-select note messages; verify chosen MIDI channel.","Do not expect analog EQ controls to emit MIDI unless manufacturer mapping confirms it."],"equipment":["Device","Known-good test signal or compatible software"],"severity":"major","pass":null}]},{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"allen-heath-xone-23","manufacturer":"Allen & Heath","model":"Xone:23C","aliases":["Xone:23","Xone 23","Xone 23C","XONE:23","XONE:23C","Allen & Heath Xone:23C","Xone:23C USB"],"category":"mixer","summary":"2+2 channel DJ mixer with 3-band total-kill EQ, VCF filters, balanced XLR main outputs, booth/record outputs and a built-in 24-bit/96 kHz four-stereo-channel USB soundcard (plus X:LINK), usable as the audio interface for Traktor Scratch Pro DVS.","identityNotes":"Confirmed by the owner: the unit is the Xone:23C (with the built-in USB soundcard), not the analog-only Xone:23. The profile id stays 'allen-heath-xone-23' so existing databases keep their unit and results. Analog layout and features are shared with the Xone:23. No MIDI DIN ports. The 23C has a USB B socket and an X:LINK port on the rear panel.","image":{"file":"allen-heath-xone-23.svg","kind":"illustration","source":"original DeckChek illustration","license":"original work","author":"DeckChek"},"documents":[{"title":"Xone:23 user manual","type":"user-manual","url":"https://www.markertek.com/Attachments/Manuals/Allen%20&%20Heath/XONE23-Manual.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Retailer hosted copy of the A&H Xone:23 manual (analog sections shared with the 23C)."},{"title":"Xone:23C user manual","type":"user-manual","url":"https://www.adorama.com/col/productManuals/AHXONE23C.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Primary manual for this unit: USB soundcard, ASIO driver install, X:LINK."},{"title":"Xone:23C brochure","type":"spec-sheet","url":"https://www.fullcompass.com/common/files/21614-AllenHeathXone23CBrochure.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Quoted specs (frequency response, THD)."},{"title":"DJ TechTools Xone:23 overview","type":"support-article","url":"https://djtechtools.com/2014/01/25/allen-heath-xone23-extended-overview","language":"en","notes":"Feature overview."},{"title":"DJ TechTools forum: 23C vs 23 + soundcard","type":"support-article","url":"https://forum.djtechtools.com/t/xone-23c-vs-xone-23-soundcard/66647","language":"en","notes":"Community comparison."},{"title":"Xone:23C user guide (A&H)","type":"user-manual","url":"https://www.allen-heath.com/content/uploads/2023/06/AP9433_5_X23C_UG.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Manufacturer-hosted guide (seen in search results, not opened)."},{"title":"Xone:23C driver release notes (v2.9.95.2)","type":"support-article","url":"https://www.allen-heath.com/content/uploads/2023/06/X23C_DSRN_29952_2.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Windows driver release notes (seen in search results, not opened); file X23C_v29952.exe."},{"title":"gehrcke.de: Xone:23C hidden technical detail and quirks","type":"support-article","url":"https://gehrcke.de/2014/07/allen-heath-xone23c-hidden-technical-detail-and-quirks/","language":"en","notes":"Community teardown of the USB send/return routing; also describes Bit accurate vs Core Audio driver modes."}],"connectivity":{"usb":{"present":true,"vendorId":null,"productIds":[],"classCompliant":null,"notes":"USB B socket on the rear panel (built-in USB soundcard). A&H's 'XONE:23C USB ASIO driver' is needed to reach all soundcard channels on Windows; the driver also offers a 'Core Audio' mode described as fully class compliant (documented for macOS; behaviour of the plain Windows class-compliant path is unverified). USB vendor/product IDs unconfirmed."},"midi":null,"audio":{"usbChannelsIn":4,"usbChannelsOut":4,"sampleRatesHz":[44100,48000,96000],"bitDepth":24,"notes":"4 stereo channels is confirmed (A&H brochure, retailers); the split of 2 stereo sends (1+2, 3+4, from the PC into the mixer) and the return/record side as 4 in / 4 out, and the exact sample-rate list, are unverified."},"analog":["2x stereo channels with phono/line","mic input (XLR)","main out balanced XLR","booth out","record out","headphone outputs","USB B (soundcard)","X:LINK"]},"drivers":[{"os":"windows","name":"Allen & Heath XONE:23C USB ASIO driver","asioName":"XONE:23C USB ASIO driver (exact ASIO entry name unverified)","deviceNamePatterns":["Xone:23C","XONE:23C","XONE:23C USB","Allen & Heath Xone"],"provider":"Allen & Heath","latestKnownVersion":"2.9.95.2 (X23C_v29952.exe, per A&H release notes found by search; check for newer)","url":"https://www.allen-heath.com/hardware/xone-series/xone23c/","required":true,"notes":"Install the A&H driver before connecting. 'Bit accurate' mode controls the audio clocks for the lowest latency and jitter; 'Core Audio' mode is class compliant and allows aggregation with other soundcards at slightly higher latency/jitter (per search summaries of the manual). Page could not be opened; confirm version and Windows 10/11 support."}],"software":[{"name":"Traktor Pro","role":"dvs","minVersion":null,"notes":"The 23C is listed as Traktor certified by retailers (e.g. https://mannys.com.au/allen-and-heath-xone-23c-traktor-certified-dj-mixer-w-usb-i-o) although another source says it is not NI approved hardware; either way Traktor Scratch Pro uses the 23C soundcard through its ASIO driver (Preferences > Audio Setup). Timecode vinyl is MK2 (owner confirmed)."}],"specs":[{"key":"freq_resp","label":"Frequency response","value":"10 Hz - 50 kHz","unit":"","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.fullcompass.com/common/files/21614-AllenHeathXone23CBrochure.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"Quoted in the 23C brochure as +/- 0 dB; analog stage shared with Xone:23."},{"key":"thd_n","label":"THD+N","value":0.01,"unit":"%","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.fullcompass.com/common/files/21614-AllenHeathXone23CBrochure.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":null},{"key":"main_noise","label":"Main mix out noise","value":-85,"unit":"dBu","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.fullcompass.com/common/files/21614-AllenHeathXone23CBrochure.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"un-weighted 22 Hz-22 kHz"},{"key":"headroom","label":"Signal headroom","value":20,"unit":"dB","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.juno.co.uk/junodaily/2014/09/24/allen-heath-xone23","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"retailer summary"},{"key":"max_out","label":"Maximum main output (balanced XLR)","value":28,"unit":"dBu","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.juno.co.uk/junodaily/2014/09/24/allen-heath-xone23","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"retailer summary"},{"key":"vcf_range","label":"VCF filter cutoff range","value":"20 Hz - 20 kHz","unit":"","tolerance":null,"source":"https://djtechtools.com/2014/01/25/allen-heath-xone23-extended-overview","confidence":"confirmed","notes":null},{"key":"eq","label":"EQ","value":"3-band total kill","unit":"","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.markertek.com/Attachments/Manuals/Allen%20&%20Heath/XONE23-Manual.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"EQ centre frequencies not confirmed"},{"key":"usb_23c","label":"USB soundcard","value":"24-bit / 96 kHz, 4 stereo channels","unit":"","tolerance":null,"source":"https://www.fullcompass.com/common/files/21614-AllenHeathXone23CBrochure.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"Built in to this unit (23C)."}],"timecode":null,"midi":null,"tests":[{"id":"x23-ch1-signal","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 1 signal health: line and phono","why":"Isolates a dead or noisy channel input stage.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"channel":1,"inputs":["line","phono"]},"steps":["Feed a stereo source into channel 1 LINE, set the input switch to LINE, trim at 12 o'clock.","Take main output (record out or master) into the PC input; run signal health.","Repeat with PHONO and a turntable."],"equipment":["Audio source","Turntable","Interface input"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch1-gain","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 1 gain structure and meter","why":"Verifies trim and fader give usable range with no clipping before the master.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play music at 0 dB; turn channel 1 trim up until the channel LED meter just peaks green/amber.","Sweep trim fully down: signal gone; fully up: no distortion at peaks if channel fader is down.","Compare to the other channel with the same source."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch1-eq","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 1 EQ and kill","why":"The Xone:23 EQs are total-kill; a kill that leaves signal means a faulty pot or switch.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play full-range music.","Turn HI fully down: highs vanish; MID fully down: mid vanishes; LO fully down: bass vanishes.","Turn each fully up: boost without distortion; centre detent is flat.","Rotate each pot slowly: no crackle or dropouts."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch1-fader","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 1 line fader","why":"Worn faders crackle or lose a channel.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play music, move the fader slowly end to end: no crackle, no channel loss, smooth travel.","Check silence at fully down."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch2-signal","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 2 signal health: line and phono","why":"Isolates a dead or noisy channel input stage.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"channel":2,"inputs":["line","phono"]},"steps":["Feed a stereo source into channel 2 LINE, set the input switch to LINE, trim at 12 o'clock.","Take main output (record out or master) into the PC input; run signal health.","Repeat with PHONO and a turntable."],"equipment":["Audio source","Turntable","Interface input"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch2-gain","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 2 gain structure and meter","why":"Verifies trim and fader give usable range with no clipping before the master.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play music at 0 dB; turn channel 2 trim up until the channel LED meter just peaks green/amber.","Sweep trim fully down: signal gone; fully up: no distortion at peaks if channel fader is down.","Compare to the other channel with the same source."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch2-eq","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 2 EQ and kill","why":"The Xone:23 EQs are total-kill; a kill that leaves signal means a faulty pot or switch.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play full-range music.","Turn HI fully down: highs vanish; MID fully down: mid vanishes; LO fully down: bass vanishes.","Turn each fully up: boost without distortion; centre detent is flat.","Rotate each pot slowly: no crackle or dropouts."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-ch2-fader","category":"mixer","title":"Channel 2 line fader","why":"Worn faders crackle or lose a channel.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play music, move the fader slowly end to end: no crackle, no channel loss, smooth travel.","Check silence at fully down."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-balance-main","category":"mixer","title":"Main output L/R balance","why":"A level mismatch between left and right output indicates a channel fault.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"output":"main"},"steps":["Play a mono 1 kHz tone through channel 1, all EQ centre.","Record main output and compare L and R."],"equipment":["1 kHz tone","Interface input"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-crosstalk","category":"cartridge","title":"Channel crosstalk through mixer","why":"Poor L/R separation or inter-channel bleed.","method":"cartridge:Channel separation","params":{"path":"mixer"},"steps":["Feed L-only signal; measure R at main out; repeat."],"equipment":["L/R test signal"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-hum","category":"safety","title":"Hum with phono connected","why":"Ground-loop hum when turntables connect to the phono input.","method":"quick:Ground & hum","params":{"input":"phono"},"steps":["Connect turntable and its ground wire to the mixer ground terminal.","Fader up, platter running, stylus lifted; run the test.","Test with the ground wire disconnected for comparison."],"equipment":["Turntable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-vcf","category":"mixer","title":"VCF filter (high-pass/low-pass) sweep","why":"The Xone filter is voltage controlled with frequency and resonance; faulty pots cause jumps.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Engage the filter on a channel / master as available.","Sweep frequency knob end to end: smooth sweep, nominal 20 Hz to 20 kHz range.","Increase resonance: self-oscillation at max is normal on Xone filters; no crackle."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-xfader","category":"mixer","title":"Crossfader: travel and curve switch","why":"Crossfader wear causes channel dropout, hence scratching noise.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Play different sources on channels 1 and 2 with assign switches set to crossfader.","Move the crossfader end to end slowly: no crackle or dropouts, both ends silent.","Flip the curve switch (gradual / sharp): cut-in point should move towards the edge.","Test with fader reverse switch if present."],"equipment":["Two sources"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-cue","category":"mixer","title":"Headphone cue and split","why":"Cue routing faults are hard to see on the main output.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Press CUE on channel 1 and then 2: only that channel is in the headphones.","Turn the cue mix / master knob: blends cue and master.","Check cue volume: no hiss at low levels, no crackle when rotating."],"equipment":["Headphones"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-outputs","category":"mixer","title":"Outputs: XLR main, booth, record","why":"Each output is a separate stage.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"outputs":["main XLR","booth","record"]},"steps":["Record each output in turn with the same source; compare levels and noise."],"equipment":["XLR/RCA cables"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-mic","category":"mixer","title":"Mic input and talkover","why":"Optional but included in channel features.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Connect a dynamic mic; speak; confirm level, EQ and no hum."],"equipment":["Microphone"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23-switches","category":"mechanical","title":"Switches, jacks and pots","why":"Dust and wear are the typical faults in mixers.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Wiggle each RCA/XLR/jack under signal: no crackle.","Toggle every input and assign switch; confirm the LED/function.","Rotate every pot through its range with music playing."],"equipment":["Music source"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23c-driver","category":"driver","title":"USB driver installed and healthy","why":"Without the A&H driver the soundcard channels are not available to Traktor.","method":"driver:check","params":{},"steps":["Connect the 23C directly to a USB port on the PC (no hub) and switch it on.","Run the driver check.","If missing, install the XONE:23C USB ASIO driver from Allen & Heath and reboot."],"equipment":["Xone:23C","USB cable"],"severity":"critical","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":{"metricId":"driver_present","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek logical presence check (not a published spec)"}},{"id":"x23c-driver-signed","category":"driver","title":"Driver signature","why":"An unsigned or legacy driver may be blocked by Windows 10/11.","method":"driver:check","params":{},"steps":["Run the driver check and read the signature result."],"equipment":["Xone:23C"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"driver_signed","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek logical presence check (not a published spec)"}},{"id":"x23c-driver-status","category":"driver","title":"Device status OK (no Code 10/43)","why":"Catches failed enumeration, power or cable faults.","method":"driver:check","params":{},"steps":["Run the driver check; open Device Manager if status is not OK."],"equipment":["Xone:23C"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"driver_status_ok","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek logical presence check (not a published spec)"}},{"id":"x23c-asio","category":"driver","title":"ASIO driver registered","why":"Traktor needs the ASIO driver to list the 23C in Preferences > Audio Setup.","method":"driver:check","params":{},"steps":["Run the driver check.","In Traktor Preferences > Audio Setup the Audio Device list should show the XONE:23C USB ASIO entry."],"equipment":["Xone:23C","Traktor Pro"],"severity":"critical","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":{"metricId":"asio_registered","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek logical presence check (not a published spec)"}},{"id":"x23c-usb-port","category":"usb","title":"USB port, cable and bus","why":"Hubs, long cables or a shared USB controller cause dropouts and clicks on the USB soundcard.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Use a short USB cable straight into the PC, not a hub.","Prefer a port on a different controller from storage devices.","Flex the cable at both connectors while audio plays: no dropouts."],"equipment":["USB cable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23c-usb-out","category":"usb","title":"USB soundcard signal health: PC to mixer (send 1+2, 3+4)","why":"Checks that the PC audio reaches the mixer USB channels, in the playback direction.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"usb":true,"direction":"out"},"steps":["Select the 23C ASIO device in the app and route a test signal to USB send 1+2, then 3+4.","Set the channel input switch to USB and record the mixer main/record output into the PC with another interface, or use the 23C return path.","Both channels must show signal at similar level, no clipping or dropouts."],"equipment":["Xone:23C","USB cable"],"severity":"major","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23c-usb-in","category":"usb","title":"USB soundcard signal health: mixer to PC (returns)","why":"Checks the record/return direction: audio the mixer sends back over USB.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"usb":true,"direction":"in"},"steps":["Feed a line or phono source into a mixer channel and set that channel/return source to USB.","Record the 23C as the input device; run signal health on each USB input pair.","Both channels must show signal at similar level, no clipping or dropouts."],"equipment":["Xone:23C","Audio source"],"severity":"major","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23c-usb-noise","category":"usb","title":"USB soundcard noise floor","why":"Idle noise or interference from the USB bus on the return channels.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"usb":true,"silence":true},"steps":["Select the 23C as input, no source playing, channel gains at normal.","Run signal health and read the noise floor."],"equipment":["Xone:23C"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"x23c-latency","category":"latency","title":"Round-trip latency at the working buffer size","why":"DVS needs low latency for tight scratching; the A&H driver trades latency against clock jitter (Bit accurate vs Core Audio modes).","method":"manual:inspection","params":{"measure":"round-trip loopback"},"steps":["Route a USB send back to a USB return through the mixer (or use a loopback via the analog outputs and another input).","Set the driver/ASIO buffer to the working setting and, in the driver panel, try Bit accurate mode for lowest latency.","In Traktor Audio Setup read the reported latency (ms); record it and any dropouts at that buffer."],"equipment":["Xone:23C","Traktor Pro"],"severity":"minor","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23c-sw-traktor","category":"software","title":"Traktor Pro install and crash/log scan","why":"Traktor crash logs often name the audio driver.","method":"software:check","params":{"software":"Traktor Pro"},"steps":["Run the software check after a play session.","Open Documents\\Native Instruments\\Traktor <ver>\\Logs for details."],"equipment":["Traktor Pro"],"severity":"minor","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":{"metricId":"software_installed","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek logical check"}},{"id":"x23c-tc-mk2-a","category":"timecode","title":"Traktor MK2 vinyl timecode on USB inputs: Deck A (33 1/3)","why":"Confirms the 23C soundcard returns a decodable quadrature timecode signal from MK2 control vinyl on this USB input pair.","method":"timecode:format-check","params":{"format":"Traktor Scratch MK2","nominalRpm":33.333333,"input":"USB return 1/2"},"steps":["Connect the turntable phono output to the mixer channel PHONO input (ground wire attached) and set the channel source so the signal is returned over USB (DVS/Traktor routing).","In the app select the 23C USB input pair 1/2 and play the MK2 timecode side at 33 1/3 rpm, pitch 0.","Run the check for at least 20 s."],"equipment":["Traktor Scratch Control Vinyl MK2","Turntable","Xone:23C"],"severity":"major","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23c-tc-mk2-b","category":"timecode","title":"Traktor MK2 vinyl timecode on USB inputs: Deck B (33 1/3)","why":"Confirms the 23C soundcard returns a decodable quadrature timecode signal from MK2 control vinyl on this USB input pair.","method":"timecode:format-check","params":{"format":"Traktor Scratch MK2","nominalRpm":33.333333,"input":"USB return 3/4"},"steps":["Connect the turntable phono output to the mixer channel PHONO input (ground wire attached) and set the channel source so the signal is returned over USB (DVS/Traktor routing).","In the app select the 23C USB input pair 3/4 and play the MK2 timecode side at 33 1/3 rpm, pitch 0.","Run the check for at least 20 s."],"equipment":["Traktor Scratch Control Vinyl MK2","Turntable","Xone:23C"],"severity":"major","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23c-tc-mk2-45","category":"timecode","title":"Traktor MK2 vinyl timecode on USB inputs at 45 rpm","why":"Speed tracking at 45 rpm through the 23C soundcard.","method":"timecode:format-check","params":{"format":"Traktor Scratch MK2","nominalRpm":45,"input":"USB return 1/2"},"steps":["Set the deck to 45 rpm and repeat the check on Deck A."],"equipment":["Traktor Scratch Control Vinyl MK2"],"severity":"minor","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23c-tc-calibrate","category":"software","title":"Timecode calibration in Traktor using the 23C","why":"The Traktor Timecode Setup scopes show whether level and phono/line gain through the mixer are right for the MK2 vinyl.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["In Traktor Preferences > Audio Setup choose the XONE:23C ASIO device; in Timecode Setup choose MK2 for each deck and assign the USB input pairs.","Play the timecode and press Calibrate; both scopes should be clean circles.","Check Absolute, Relative and Internal modes by loading a track."],"equipment":["Traktor Pro","Traktor Scratch Control Vinyl MK2"],"severity":"major","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null},{"id":"x23-dvs-line","category":"dvs","title":"DVS through the mixer line inputs (external interface)","why":"Alternative path: when an external interface (e.g. Audio 8 DJ) is used instead of the 23C soundcard, timecode passes through the LINE inputs.","method":"dvs:DVS signal","params":{},"steps":["Connect the Traktor interface outputs to mixer channel LINE inputs and play a deck.","Play control vinyl on a turntable into the interface and confirm the returned deck audio is clean on the mixer channel."],"equipment":["Audio interface","Control vinyl"],"severity":"minor","software":"Traktor Pro","pass":null}]},{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"alphatheta-ddj-flx10","manufacturer":"AlphaTheta","model":"DDJ-FLX10","category":"controller","summary":"controller profile with jog, pad, fader, eq, audio, usb diagnostic groups. Companion workflow(s): rekordbox,Serato DJ Pro.","identityNotes":"Research seed; the manufacturer's DDJ-FLX10 Instruction Manual DRI1822D documents USB MIDI control (p. 179) and a 44.1 kHz audio section with 24-bit A/D and D/A converters (p. 175). Converter depth and a nominal audio sampling rate do not establish a complete USB format/rate list or channel counts, which remain unknown. USB IDs, class compliance, exact control maps, hardware/firmware revision, current OS/driver compatibility and physical performance remain unverified; no factory pass tolerances are inferred.","documents":[{"title":"Manufacturer detailed product feature and specifications","type":"manual","url":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/product/dj-controllers/ddj-flx10/","language":"en"},{"title":"Manufacturer manual/product documentation","type":"manual","url":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/support/","language":"en","notes":"Direct manual for some models; otherwise manufacturer's product/support landing page. Verify exact variant."},{"title":"Firmware, driver and downloads","type":"driver","url":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/support/","language":"en","notes":"Check the model-specific download page and operating system."},{"title":"Manufacturer support","type":"support-article","url":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/support/","language":"en","notes":"Official source entry point."},{"title":"Service manual (public availability not established)","type":"service-manual","url":"","notes":"Do not substitute operating instructions for a service manual."},{"title":"MIDI implementation chart (not verified)","type":"midi-message-list","url":"","notes":"Use MIDI Learn or the published mapping; HID events may not appear as MIDI."},{"title":"DDJ-FLX10 Instruction Manual (DRI1822D)","type":"user-manual","url":"https://downloads.support.alphatheta.com/manuals/dj-controllers/DDJ-FLX10/DDJ-FLX10_DRI1822D_manual.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Manufacturer manual; support listing dated 23 October 2024; checked 2026-11-18. USB MIDI control: p. 179; audio-section sampling rate and converter depth: p. 175. These are documented capabilities, not physical or current-platform qualification."}],"connectivity":{"usb":{"present":true,"vendorId":null,"productIds":[],"classCompliant":null},"midi":{"usbMidi":true,"din":null,"portNamePatterns":["DDJ-FLX10"]},"audio":{"usbChannelsIn":null,"usbChannelsOut":null,"sampleRatesHz":[],"bitDepth":null}},"software":[{"name":"rekordbox","role":"claimed companion / operating mode; verify model and version","minVersion":null},{"name":"Serato DJ Pro","role":"claimed companion / operating mode; verify model and version","minVersion":null}],"specs":[{"key":"candidate_capabilities","label":"Candidate hardware functions for diagnostic planning","value":"jog, pad, fader, eq, audio, usb","unit":"","source":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/support/","confidence":"unverified","notes":"These category-level capabilities require checking the exact hardware documentation."},{"key":"verified_channels","label":"channels","value":4,"unit":"count","source":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/product/dj-controllers/ddj-flx10/","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"Source model page; inspect revision for deviations."},{"key":"verified_track_separation","label":"track separation","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/product/dj-controllers/ddj-flx10/","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"Source model page; inspect revision for deviations."},{"key":"verified_dmx_output","label":"dmx output","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://www.pioneerdj.com/en/product/dj-controllers/ddj-flx10/","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"Source model page; inspect revision for deviations."},{"key":"verified_usb_midi_transport","label":"USB MIDI control transport","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://downloads.support.alphatheta.com/manuals/dj-controllers/DDJ-FLX10/DDJ-FLX10_DRI1822D_manual.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"DRI1822D p. 179. The unit can contro