tting Started 2.7.7, section 2.3.5, p. 30 and p. 31: separate 5-pin DIN IN and OUT connect external MIDI equipment. Activate the ports in MIDI Preferences for standalone software, or configure the host for plug-in use. USB MIDI remains unresolved.","documents":[{"title":"MASCHINE MK3 product features and audio interface specifications","type":"spec-sheet","url":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","language":"en","notes":"Checked 2026-11-18. Exact MK3 hardware: 24-bit audio interface with a 96 kHz maximum. This does not enumerate all supported hardware sample rates."},{"title":"MASCHINE MK3 Getting Started, software 2.7.7","type":"user-manual","url":"https://www.native-instruments.com/fileadmin/ni_media/downloads/manuals/maschine_277/MASCHINE_MK3_Getting_Started_English_2_7_7.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Checked 2026-11-18. Document identifies software 2.7.7 (07/2018) and MASCHINE MK3 hardware. Section 2.1, printed pp. 17-18, covers USB computer connection; section 2.2.1, p. 21, routes inputs L/R to 1/2, main outputs to 1/2 and headphones to 3/4. The software/document version is not a firmware qualification."},{"title":"Driver and firmware support","type":"driver","url":"https://www.native-instruments.com/en/support/downloads/","language":"en","notes":"Confirm OS-specific driver and version."},{"title":"Notes on MASCHINE MK3's audio interface","type":"support-article","url":"https://support.native-instruments.com/support/solutions/articles/69000879608-notes-on-maschine-mk3-s-audio-interface","language":"en","notes":"Checked 2026-11-18; no article revision identified. Connecting a microphone disables the line inputs; they are not simultaneous independent input channels. Main and headphone playback are separately addressable."},{"title":"Service manual","type":"service-manual","url":"","notes":"Not found/verified as publicly available."},{"title":"MIDI/HID map","type":"midi-message-list","url":"","notes":"Exact implementation mapping not verified; use learn mode and capture."},{"title":"Native Instruments MASCHINE MK3 Getting Started — 2.7.7 (MASCHINE MK3 MIDI scope)","type":"user-manual","url":"https://docs.native-instruments.com/pdf-guides/maschine_277/MASCHINE_MK3_Getting_Started_English_2_7_7.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Transport evidence only. 2.7.7; p. 30; p. 31. Exact MASCHINE MK3 DIN IN and OUT. The 2.7.7 document/software edition is not a firmware qualification. USB MIDI remains unresolved."}],"connectivity":{"usb":{"present":true,"vendorId":null,"productIds":[],"classCompliant":null},"midi":{"usbMidi":null,"din":true,"portNamePatterns":["MASCHINE MK3"]},"audio":{"usbChannelsIn":2,"usbChannelsOut":4,"sampleRatesHz":[],"bitDepth":24}},"software":[{"name":"MASCHINE","role":"companion or operating mode; exact compatibility pending verification","minVersion":null}],"specs":[{"key":"candidate_capabilities","label":"Candidate hardware test groups","value":"pad,encoder,button,usb,display,audio","unit":"","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/en/support/downloads/","confidence":"unverified","notes":"Model-dependent test planner; not exact control count or specification."},{"key":"verified_velocity_sensitive_pads","label":"velocity sensitive pads","value":16,"unit":"count","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_touch_knobs","label":"touch knobs","value":8,"unit":"count","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_color_displays","label":"color displays","value":2,"unit":"count","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_audio_sample_rate_max","label":"audio sample rate max","value":96000,"unit":"Hz","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_audio_bit_depth","label":"audio bit depth","value":24,"unit":"bit","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_usb_audio_input_channels","label":"USB audio input channels","value":2,"unit":"count","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/fileadmin/ni_media/downloads/manuals/maschine_277/MASCHINE_MK3_Getting_Started_English_2_7_7.pdf section 2.2.1, printed p. 21","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"MASCHINE MK3 input channels 1/2 are the left/right pair; the microphone and line-input paths share this pair. Software version 2.7.7 (07/2018) identifies the guide, not qualified firmware."},{"key":"verified_usb_audio_output_channels","label":"USB audio output channels","value":4,"unit":"count","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/fileadmin/ni_media/downloads/manuals/maschine_277/MASCHINE_MK3_Getting_Started_English_2_7_7.pdf section 2.2.1, printed p. 21","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"The selected MASCHINE MK3 audio device routes main left/right to 1/2 and headphone left/right to 3/4. MASCHINE software's virtual output buses do not establish additional hardware channels."},{"key":"verified_smart_strip","label":"smart strip","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://www.native-instruments.com/products/maschine","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_din_midi_transport","label":"Documented DIN MIDI transport","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://docs.native-instruments.com/pdf-guides/maschine_277/MASCHINE_MK3_Getting_Started_English_2_7_7.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"MASCHINE MK3 Getting Started 2.7.7, section 2.3.5, p. 30 and p. 31: separate 5-pin DIN IN and OUT connect external MIDI equipment. Activate the ports in MIDI Preferences for standalone software, or configure the host for plug-in use. USB MIDI remains unresolved."}],"midi":{"mapSource":"learn","complete":false,"controls":[]},"tests":[{"id":"native-instruments-maschine-mk3-pad","category":"midi","title":"Pad trigger and LED coverage","why":"Test actual hardware response without inventing MIDI IDs, audio tolerances or H