thout the Pioneer DJ ASIO driver the device falls back to generic Windows audio (high latency, missing channels) or does not appear in DJ software.","method":"driver:check","params":{},"steps":["Connect the device by USB and power it on.","Run the check; it matches Device Manager names against the profile.","If not present, install the current driver from Pioneer DJ support and reboot."],"equipment":["USB cable","Windows PC"],"severity":"critical","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"driver_present","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-driver-signed","category":"driver","title":"Driver signed, status OK and ASIO registered","why":"Unsigned or errored drivers cause crackles, disconnects and ASIO devices missing from the DJ software audio menu.","method":"driver:check","params":{"focus":"signed,status,asio"},"steps":["Run the driver check after the device is powered.","Review signed / status / ASIO registration results."],"equipment":["Windows PC"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"driver_status_ok","op":"equals","value":1,"value2":null,"unit":"bool","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-firmware","category":"software","title":"PLX-CRSS12 firmware version up to date","why":"Old firmware can cause MIDI/jog/DVS faults fixed in later releases.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Open the Pioneer DJ firmware/updater utility for PLX-CRSS12, or the DJ software settings page that shows firmware.","Note installed firmware version and compare with latest on the Pioneer DJ support page (not auto-checked; version unverified in research).","Tick when firmware is current or update completed."],"equipment":["Pioneer DJ support firmware download"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-software-rekordbox","category":"software","title":"rekordbox installed, no recent crashes","why":"Crashes or log errors in rekordbox often explain dropouts that look like hardware faults.","method":"software:check","params":{"software":"rekordbox"},"steps":["Run the rekordbox log scan.","Review crash count (90 days) and log errors."],"equipment":["rekordbox"],"severity":"major","software":"rekordbox","pass":{"metricId":"software_crashes_90d","op":"<=","value":0,"value2":null,"unit":"count","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-software-serato","category":"software","title":"Serato DJ Pro installed, no recent crashes","why":"Crashes or log errors in Serato DJ Pro often explain dropouts that look like hardware faults.","method":"software:check","params":{"software":"Serato DJ Pro"},"steps":["Run the Serato DJ Pro log scan.","Review crash count (90 days) and log errors."],"equipment":["Serato DJ Pro"],"severity":"major","software":"Serato DJ Pro","pass":{"metricId":"software_crashes_90d","op":"<=","value":0,"value2":null,"unit":"count","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-usb-audio","category":"audio","title":"USB audio return (DVS signal) signal health","why":"Confirms the USB audio path delivers a clean, level-balanced stereo signal into the DJ software.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"inputs":"PLX-CRSS12 USB"},"steps":["Connect the CRSS12 via USB-C and select it as audio device in rekordbox or Serato.","Set the deck to digital vinyl/DVS mode and press START.","Run Signal health on the CRSS12 USB input for 10 seconds."],"equipment":["USB-C cable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-analog-out","category":"audio","title":"Analog PHONO/LINE output signal health (both channels)","why":"Checks the analog output path (RCA) for channel loss, imbalance or noise independent of USB.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{"inputs":"mixer channel fed by CRSS12"},"steps":["Connect the CRSS12 RCA output to a mixer line/phono input and set the input selector accordingly (check the PHONO/LINE switch on the unit).","Play a known record or test record.","Run Signal health on that mixer channel."],"equipment":["Mixer or audio interface","Test record"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-ground-hum","category":"safety","title":"Ground and hum check (analog out)","why":"A missing ground wire or bad RCA cable produces 50/60 Hz hum.","method":"quick:Ground & hum","params":{},"steps":["Connect the analog output and the ground lead to the mixer GND post (ground lead behaviour for this model unverified).","Lower the tonearm onto an inactive area / lift tonearm and play.","Run Ground & hum; compare with ground lead connected and removed."],"equipment":["Mixer","RCA and ground leads"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-vibration","category":"mechanical","title":"Motor and bearing vibration","why":"Platter or motor vibration feeds rumble to the cartridge and the timecode signal.","method":"quick:Vibration","params":{},"steps":["Place the turntable on a stable surface with feet adjusted.","Run Vibration with platter spinning at 33 rpm, then 45 rpm, tonearm lifted."],"equipment":["Test record optional"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-speed-33","category":"speed","title":"Speed accuracy at 33 1/3 rpm (pitch 0%)","why":"Checks the quartz-locked motor against nominal speed.","method":"speed:Speed & pitch","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333,"referenceHz":1000,"pitchPosition":0},"steps":["Set speed to 33 rpm and pitch to 0 (centre click).","Play a 1 kHz test record or, in Digital Vinyl mode, the generated timecode through the speed test.","Run the test for 30 seconds."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-speed-45","category":"speed","title":"Speed accuracy at 45 rpm (pitch 0%)","why":"Checks 45 rpm quartz lock.","method":"speed:Speed & pitch","params":{"nominalRpm":45,"referenceHz":1000,"pitchPosition":0},"steps":["Set speed to 45 rpm, pitch 0.","Run the test for 30 seconds."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-pitch-map-8","category":"pitch","title":"Pitch map, range ±8%","why":"Verifies the slider tracks linearly and reaches ±8% (documented range).","method":"speed:Pitch map","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333,"range":8,"pitchPositions":[-8,-4,0,4,8]},"steps":["Select the ±8% range.","At each listed slider position run the Pitch map step.","Review error per position."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-pitch-map-16","category":"pitch","title":"Pitch map, range ±16%","why":"Verifies ±16% range.","method":"speed:Pitch map","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333,"range":16,"pitchPositions":[-16,-8,0,8,16]},"steps":["Select ±16%.","Run each position."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-pitch-map-50","category":"pitch","title":"Pitch map, range ±50%","why":"Verifies ±50% wide range, used for scratch/tape-stop effects.","method":"speed:Pitch map","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333,"range":50,"pitchPositions":[-50,-25,0,25,50]},"steps":["Select ±50%.","Run each position."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-quartz-lock","category":"speed","title":"Quartz lock stability","why":"The platter should hold speed at pitch 0 with quartz lock engaged; drift indicates motor/PLL faults.","method":"speed:Quartz lock","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333},"steps":["Enable quartz lock if the unit has a toggle (unverified for this model).","Run Quartz lock for 2 minutes at 33 rpm."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-warmup","category":"speed","title":"Warm-up speed drift","why":"Motor drifting as it warms indicates driver faults.","method":"speed:Warm-up speed","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333,"durationMin":15},"steps":["Start from cold, run at 33 rpm.","Run Warm-up speed for 15 minutes."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-startstop","category":"speed","title":"Start time and brake","why":"Spec states 0.3 s start time; slow or lazy start/brake indicates motor or torque issues.","method":"speed:Startup & brake","params":{"nominalRpm":33.333333},"steps":["Stop the platter, press START/STOP; run Startup & brake.","Compare start time to the 0.3 s figure (retailer-quoted; official unverified)."],"equipment":["1 kHz test record or timecode"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-tc-serato","category":"timecode","title":"Internal Digital Vinyl signal: Serato mode","why":"Verifies the internally generated control signal is clean for Serato DJ Pro.","method":"timecode:format-check","params":{"format":"Serato CV02.5","nominalRpm":33.333333},"steps":["Connect USB, open Serato DJ Pro, set the deck to Digital Vinyl mode.","Press START/STOP so the platter spins.","Run format-check on the USB input. Format shown is an assumption (Serato CV02.5); see research notes."],"equipment":["USB-C cable"],"severity":"major","software":"Serato DJ Pro","pass":null},{"id":"crss12-tc-rb","category":"timecode","title":"Internal Digital Vinyl signal: rekordbox mode","why":"Verifies the control signal is clean for rekordbox DVS.","method":"timecode:format-check","params":{"format":"rekordbox DVS","nominalRpm":33.333333},"steps":["Connect USB, open rekordbox in Performance mode and enable the CRSS12 deck.","Press START/STOP.","Run format-check. The exact rekordbox format name is unverified."],"equipment":["USB-C cable"],"severity":"major","software":"rekordbox","pass":null},{"id":"crss12-dvs-serato","category":"dvs","title":"DVS signal integrity in Serato DJ Pro","why":"Dropouts or channel imbalance cause the track to skip or lose position.","method":"dvs:DVS signal","params":{},"steps":["Digital Vinyl mode in Serato; spin the platter, then scratch back and forth for 20 seconds.","Run DVS signal."],"equipment":["USB-C cable"],"severity":"major","software":"Serato DJ Pro","pass":null},{"id":"crss12-dvs-rb","category":"dvs","title":"DVS signal integrity in rekordbox","why":"Same as above for rekordbox.","method":"dvs:DVS signal","params":{},"steps":["Enable DVS in rekordbox.","Spin and scratch for 20 seconds.","Run DVS signal."],"equipment":["USB-C cable"],"severity":"major","software":"rekordbox","pass":null},{"id":"crss12-dvs-scratch-sw","category":"dvs","title":"Scratch response and platter touch","why":"Platter touch/motion should map to track position without lag.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["In each software, load a track and hold the platter: track should stop; release: track resumes.","Back-cue and forward-cue at slow speed and check for stutter, drift or position jumps.","Tick if response is immediate with no skipping."],"equipment":[],"severity":"major","software":"Serato DJ Pro","pass":null},{"id":"crss12-midi-coverage","category":"midi","title":"MIDI coverage: every control reports","why":"A dead control (broken pot, fader track, switch, pad) never sends MIDI.","method":"midi:coverage","params":{"groups":["Deck","Pads"]},"steps":["Open the MIDI test and select this device's MIDI port.","Exercise every control once in sequence, each pad/button/knob/fader.","Review any control not seen and any unexpected message."],"equipment":["USB cable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"midi_controls_seen_percent","op":">=","value":100,"value2":null,"unit":"%","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-button-bounce","category":"midi","title":"Switch bounce / stuck check (START/STOP, pads, mode buttons)","why":"Worn switches double-trigger (bounce) or stick, causing false cue/play triggers.","method":"midi:button","params":{"controlIds":[]},"steps":["Press each button/pad once firmly, then once lightly.","Hold one for 3 seconds then release.","Review bounce count and stuck state."],"equipment":["USB cable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"midi_button_stuck","op":"equals","value":0,"value2":null,"unit":"count","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-led","category":"midi","title":"Performance pad and button LEDs light correctly","why":"Dead LEDs hide state (cue, loop, pad bank).","method":"midi:led","params":{"controlIds":[]},"steps":["Start the LED test; the app lights each LED.","Confirm each lights and has the expected colour/brightness; mark failures."],"equipment":[],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-jog-platter","category":"midi","title":"Platter (MIDI/DVS motion): ticks per revolution and direction","why":"Encoder/optical faults give missing ticks or reversed counts that cause scratch and nudge errors.","method":"midi:jog","params":{"controlId":"platter"},"steps":["Rotate Platter (MIDI/DVS motion) one slow revolution clockwise, then one counter-clockwise.","Review ticks per revolution and direction errors."],"equipment":["USB cable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":{"metricId":"midi_jog_direction_errors","op":"equals","value":0,"value2":null,"unit":"count","source":"DeckChek test definition (not a manufacturer spec)"}},{"id":"crss12-fader-pitch","category":"midi","title":"Pitch fader: full travel, monotonic, low jitter","why":"Worn tracks or dirty pots cause jumps, dead zones or jitter. Spec ranges ±8/±16/±50%.","method":"midi:fader","params":{"controlId":"pitch"},"steps":["Move Pitch fader slowly end to end, then back, three times.","Pause at the middle for 2 seconds.","Review min/max, monotonicity, jitter and resolution."],"equipment":["USB cable"],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-midi-jitter","category":"midi","title":"MIDI timing jitter under constant motion","why":"Timing jitter or USB hub congestion makes jogs/scratching feel uneven.","method":"midi:latency","params":{},"steps":["Connect the device directly to a PC USB port (no hub).","Rotate the main continuous control at a steady speed for 10 seconds.","Review inter-message jitter."],"equipment":["USB cable"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-platter","category":"mechanical","title":"Platter and spindle inspection","why":"Damage to the platter or the magnet clamp affects the generated signal and speed.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Platter sits flat, no wobble or rubbing.","Slipmat present, not worn or ripped.","Spindle / MAGVEL-CLAMP intact, no looseness (clamp described by reviewers; unverified in manual)."],"equipment":[],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-tonearm","category":"mechanical","title":"Tonearm, headshell and cartridge","why":"Tonearm play or a damaged stylus degrades analog playback and tracking.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Tonearm moves freely vertically and laterally with no play.","Headshell connectors secure, wires tight.","Stylus tip clean, no bent cantilever.","Counterweight and anti-skate settings match the cartridge."],"equipment":[],"severity":"major","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-controls","category":"mechanical","title":"Controls, pads, pitch fader and connectors","why":"Worn pads, faders or USB-C and RCA ports cause dropouts.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Pads and buttons click evenly, none sticky.","Pitch fader smooth with a centre detent, no scratchiness.","Start-Stop, speed select and range buttons respond.","USB-C port and RCA/ground connectors firm, no wobble.","Feet and body: no cracks, dust cover seated."],"equipment":[],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null},{"id":"crss12-cartridge-channel","category":"cartridge","title":"Cartridge channel check (analog)","why":"Detects dead or reversed channel in the analog path.","method":"cartridge:Channel & cartridge","params":{},"steps":["Play a channel-check test record on the analog output.","Run Channel & cartridge."],"equipment":["Test record"],"severity":"minor","software":null,"pass":null}]},{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"rane-four","manufacturer":"RANE","model":"FOUR","category":"controller","summary":"controller profile with jog, pad, fader, eq, audio, usb diagnostic groups. Companion workflow(s): Serato DJ Pro.","identityNotes":"Research seed with conservative, capability-dependent tests. Exact MIDI IDs, USB IDs, revision, OS support, audio channel maps and tolerance limits are NOT verified; learn or confirm on real hardware before giving pass/fail based on fixed specifications. Research update (2026-11-18 UTC): FOUR User Guide v1.0 documents USB MIDI with USB A/B source selection. Converter and DSP specifications do not establish the supported USB stream formats; audio counts, rates and scalar USB bit depth remain unknown.","documents":[{"title":"Manufacturer model documentation and feature FAQ","type":"support-article","url":"https://support.rane.com/en/support/solutions/articles/69000828752-rane-four-frequently-asked-questions","language":"en"},{"title":"Manufacturer manual/product documentation","type":"manual","url":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","language":"en","notes":"Direct manual for some models; otherwise manufacturer's product/support landing page. Verify exact variant."},{"title":"Firmware, driver and downloads","type":"driver","url":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","language":"en","notes":"Check the model-specific download page and operating system."},{"title":"Manufacturer support","type":"support-article","url":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","language":"en","notes":"Official source entry point."},{"title":"Service manual (public availability not established)","type":"service-manual","url":"","notes":"Do not substitute operating instructions for a service manual."},{"title":"MIDI implementation chart (not verified)","type":"midi-message-list","url":"","notes":"Use MIDI Learn or the published mapping; HID events may not appear as MIDI."},{"title":"FOUR User Guide v1.0","type":"user-manual","url":"https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/rane/four/FOUR%20-%20User%20Guide%20-%20v1.0.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Checked 2026-11-18 UTC. Pages 12 and 15 document USB MIDI and source selection; page 35 labels converter and DSP specifications separately. Document version is not firmware qualification."}],"connectivity":{"usb":{"present":true,"vendorId":null,"productIds":[],"classCompliant":null},"midi":{"usbMidi":true,"din":null,"portNamePatterns":["FOUR"]},"audio":{"usbChannelsIn":null,"usbChannelsOut":null,"sampleRatesHz":[],"bitDepth":null}},"software":[{"name":"Serato DJ Pro","role":"claimed companion / operating mode; verify model and version","minVersion":null}],"specs":[{"key":"candidate_capabilities","label":"Candidate hardware functions for diagnostic planning","value":"jog, pad, fader, eq, audio, usb","unit":"","source":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","confidence":"unverified","notes":"These category-level capabilities require checking the exact hardware documentation."},{"key":"verified_controller_channels","label":"controller channels","value":4,"unit":"count","source":"https://support.rane.com/en/support/solutions/articles/69000828752-rane-four-frequently-asked-questions","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_stem_split","label":"stem split","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://support.rane.com/en/support/solutions/articles/69000828752-rane-four-frequently-asked-questions","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_serato_stems_supported","label":"serato stems supported","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://support.rane.com/en/support/solutions/articles/69000828752-rane-four-frequently-asked-questions","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_algoriddim_djay_supported","label":"algoriddim djay supported","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://support.rane.com/en/support/solutions/articles/69000828752-rane-four-frequently-asked-questions","confidence":"confirmed"},{"key":"verified_usb_midi_transport","label":"USB MIDI transport","value":true,"unit":"bool","source":"https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/rane/four/FOUR%20-%20User%20Guide%20-%20v1.0.pdf","confidence":"confirmed","notes":"USB A/B and USB/Line selection govern the associated channel/deck MIDI path."}],"midi":{"mapSource":"learn","complete":false,"controls":[]},"tests":[{"id":"rane-four-jog","category":"midi","title":"Jog rotation and touch","why":"Check jog function on FOUR; avoid assumptions about HID or analog routing.","method":"midi:jog","params":{},"steps":["Consult the exact FOUR manual for the relevant connectors and operating mode.","Exercise each jog element on the device and observe MIDI, HID/software response or audio measurement as applicable.","Check slow and fast transitions, all channels/sides, and repeats; save raw evidence and mark unobservable functions as not tested."],"equipment":["Connected device","Compatible host software or capture interface when required"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-pad","category":"midi","title":"Pad and mode coverage","why":"Check pad function on FOUR; avoid assumptions about HID or analog routing.","method":"midi:button","params":{},"steps":["Consult the exact FOUR manual for the relevant connectors and operating mode.","Exercise each pad element on the device and observe MIDI, HID/software response or audio measurement as applicable.","Check slow and fast transitions, all channels/sides, and repeats; save raw evidence and mark unobservable functions as not tested."],"equipment":["Connected device","Compatible host software or capture interface when required"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-fader","category":"mixer","title":"Fader endpoint and continuity","why":"Check fader function on FOUR; avoid assumptions about HID or analog routing.","method":"midi:fader","params":{},"steps":["Consult the exact FOUR manual for the relevant connectors and operating mode.","Exercise each fader element on the device and observe MIDI, HID/software response or audio measurement as applicable.","Check slow and fast transitions, all channels/sides, and repeats; save raw evidence and mark unobservable functions as not tested."],"equipment":["Connected device","Compatible host software or capture interface when required"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-eq","category":"mixer","title":"EQ and trim range","why":"Check eq function on FOUR; avoid assumptions about HID or analog routing.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Consult the exact FOUR manual for the relevant connectors and operating mode.","Exercise each eq element on the device and observe MIDI, HID/software response or audio measurement as applicable.","Check slow and fast transitions, all channels/sides, and repeats; save raw evidence and mark unobservable functions as not tested."],"equipment":["Connected device","Compatible host software or capture interface when required"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-audio","category":"audio","title":"Audio output and cue channel integrity","why":"Check audio function on FOUR; avoid assumptions about HID or analog routing.","method":"quick:Signal health","params":{},"steps":["Consult the exact FOUR manual for the relevant connectors and operating mode.","Exercise each audio element on the device and observe MIDI, HID/software response or audio measurement as applicable.","Check slow and fast transitions, all channels/sides, and repeats; save raw evidence and mark unobservable functions as not tested."],"equipment":["Connected device","Compatible host software or capture interface when required"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-usb","category":"usb","title":"USB detection and reconnection","why":"Check usb function on FOUR; avoid assumptions about HID or analog routing.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Consult the exact FOUR manual for the relevant connectors and operating mode.","Exercise each usb element on the device and observe MIDI, HID/software response or audio measurement as applicable.","Check slow and fast transitions, all channels/sides, and repeats; save raw evidence and mark unobservable functions as not tested."],"equipment":["Connected device","Compatible host software or capture interface when required"],"severity":"major","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-firmware","category":"software","title":"Firmware and application compatibility","why":"Prevent mismatched firmware and software versions from being reported as hardware failure.","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Read installed firmware and hardware revision.","Compare with the model-specific official compatibility and downloads pages.","Record operating system, application version, firmware and documentation URL."],"equipment":["Manufacturer documentation"],"severity":"minor","pass":null},{"id":"rane-four-verified-mode-check","title":"Stem Split channel routing and source selectors","category":"software","method":"manual:inspection","params":{},"steps":["Run compatible Serato DJ Pro and load a reference track.","Activate Stem Split and verify vocals route to channel 1/2 and instruments to 3/4.","Verify source selectors USB and balanced gain settings, then unsplit."],"equipment":["Known-good media","Compatible OS / software"],"severity":"major","pass":null}]},{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"rane-one","manufacturer":"RANE","model":"ONE","category":"controller","summary":"controller profile with jog, motor, pad, fader, eq, audio, usb diagnostic groups. Companion workflow(s): Serato DJ Pro.","identityNotes":"Research seed with conservative, capability-dependent tests. Exact MIDI IDs, USB IDs, revision, OS support, audio channel maps and tolerance limits are NOT verified; learn or confirm on real hardware before giving pass/fail based on fixed specifications. Transport addendum (2026-11-18): RANE ONE User Guide v1.5, p. 5 and p. 9: original ONE rear USB-B ports carry MIDI. Deck controls send MIDI only with the deck source at USB A/B. ONE MKII behavior is not imported.","documents":[{"title":"Manufacturer model feature reference","type":"support-article","url":"https://support.rane.com/en/support/solutions/articles/69000871126-rane-one-x-rane-one-mkii-what-are-the-differences-","language":"en","notes":["Original RANE ONE: motorized 7-inch platters, 16 pads, dual USB soundcards. Do not add ONE MKII exclusive internal FX, OLED or Precision Feel upgrades."]},{"title":"Manufacturer manual/product documentation","type":"manual","url":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","language":"en","notes":"Direct manual for some models; otherwise manufacturer's product/support landing page. Verify exact variant."},{"title":"Firmware, driver and downloads","type":"driver","url":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","language":"en","notes":"Check the model-specific download page and operating system."},{"title":"Manufacturer support","type":"support-article","url":"https://www.rane.com/downloads","language":"en","notes":"Official source entry point."},{"title":"Service manual (public availability not established)","type":"service-manual","url":"","notes":"Do not substitute operating instructions for a service manual."},{"title":"MIDI implementation chart (not verified)","type":"midi-message-list","url":"","notes":"Use MIDI Learn or the published mapping; HID events may not appear as MIDI."},{"title":"RANE ONE User Guide — v1.5 (ONE MIDI scope)","type":"user-manual","url":"https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/rane/one/RANE-ONE-User-Guide-v1_5.pdf","language":"en","notes":"Transport evidence only. v1.5; p. 5; p. 9. Original ONE, excluding ONE MKII. The deck source must be USB A/B for deck-control MIDI."}],"connectivity":{"usb":{"present":true,"vendorId":null,"productIds":[],"classCompliant":null},"midi":{"usbMidi":true,"din